# QuantiumV regression test list.
# Columns (| separated, no | inside a field): tag | testbench | extra
# files (comma-separated, may be empty) | cwd (design or testbench) |
# cores (comma-separated subset of ref,pipe) | expect (pass, or
# xfail:<reason>) | timeout seconds (blank = script default) | extra
# iverilog flags (optional, e.g. -P parameter overrides).
# Blank lines and #-comments ignored.
#
# "cores" names the builds a test is meaningful for (run_regress.sh --core):
#   pipe  the main build, the pipelined core in design/pipe/ -- every row
#   ref   the frozen multi-cycle reference, verification/reference/ref_core.sv
#         (named `core` by -DQV_REF_AS_CORE) -- 78 rows
# run_regress.sh --core X SKIPS any row not listing X, silently, so a row that
# names neither core would just never run: there must be 136 rows listing pipe.
#
# The rows that omit ref are the design/*_tb.sv unit tests of a leaf module
# (alu, c_expand, csr_file, divider, register_file) and of the divider's
# kill input, which instantiate the module by its fixed name -- the reference's
# ref_* counterparts have no such name alias, unlike ref_core.sv, which answers
# to `core` -- and the design/pipe/*_tb.sv module tests.
#
# A testbench that looks at the core's internals has one half for each core:
# `ifndef QV_REF_AS_CORE takes the pipelined core's, the else half is the
# reference's (state, fstate, TLB registers, ...). A new white-box test does
# the same, so it runs on both.

# === design/*_tb.sv ===
design_alu_tb|design/alu_tb.sv||design|pipe|pass|
design_c_expand_tb|design/c_expand_tb.sv||design|pipe|pass|
design_cache_complex_tb|design/cache_complex_tb.sv||design|ref,pipe|pass|
